  "roll_handling": {
    "mechanism": "EIA's 'Contract 1' label is itself auto-rolling: it always denotes the nearest unexpired delivery month as of that trading date, per EIA's TblDefs page. Reading the c1 column day-over-day therefore yields a paper-rolled, zero-slippage front-month series with the delivery-month switch occurring invisibly at each contract's calendar expiry -- no explicit roll-date logic is needed on our side, and no look-ahead is introduced because c1(t) only reflects what NYMEX listed as the nearest contract as of date t.",
    "expiry_rules_source": "EIA TblDefs pages (pet_pri_fut_tbldef2.asp and NG equivalent), reproduced in reports/eia_futures/REPORT.md sec 2",
    "look_ahead_risk": "None identified in the c1 construction itself. A caveat: this produces an idealized (cost-free, slippage-free) roll -- it is not tradable as-is (see limitations)."
  },
